The Kernel class is not found in the expected location. Since the Kernel class is central and the LoggerFactory property is read-only, I cannot directly assign a logger to it. The method under test uses kernel.LoggerFactory.CreateLogger to get a logger, so to capture logs, I need to create a Kernel instance with a LoggerFactory that uses a custom ILoggerProvider capturing warnings.

I will write tests that create a Kernel instance (using the default constructor or a factory method if available) and inject a LoggerFactory with a custom ILoggerProvider that captures warnings. Then I will call the method and verify that the expected warnings are logged.

I will submit a test file that:
- Creates a custom ILoggerProvider capturing warnings.
- Creates a LoggerFactory with that provider.
- Creates a Kernel instance (using a default constructor or a factory method).
- Uses reflection or other means to set the LoggerFactory if possible.
- Calls CreatePluginFromCopilotAgentPluginAsync with a crafted plugin file that triggers the warning on line 114.
- Asserts that the warning "No API description URL found in the runtime object." is logged.

I will submit this test now.

